9. Handling the Big Paragraph and (a)

We’ll save it in four different variables using naming conventions.

const loremText = "Lorem ipsum ... (long text)";     // camelCase
const LOREM_TEXT = "Lorem ipsum ... (long text)";    // UPPER_CASE
let lorem_text = "Lorem ipsum ... (long text)";      // snake_case
var LoremText = "Lorem ipsum ... (long text)";       // PascalCase


Now, wherever there’s (a), perform the following replacements:

let modifiedText = loremText
  .replaceAll("(a)", "\n")        // new line
  .replaceAll("(a)", "\t")        // tab
  .replaceAll("(a)", "\\")        // backslash
  .replaceAll("(a)", "\'")        // single quote
  .replaceAll("(a)", "\"")        // double quote
  .replaceAll("(a)", ":")         // colon mark
  .replaceAll("(a)", "//");       // double slash


(In real usage, you’d pick one replacement per requirement.)

